chat_seq.py: error: --temp 0.9: sampling needs the on-chip top-k capture unit, which arrives with the next RTL rung (rung 4).  The board is running a bitstream without it, so there is no candidate set to sample from.  Greedy decode is unaffected; --verify-head still cross-checks the chip's head against the host copy.
  Pass --topk-base <addr> once the rung-4 bitstream is on the board; until then --temp 0 (greedy) is the only decode this build can do — and it is bit-exact.
